<problem boxed>
  <setup>
    <selectFromSequence name="a" from="2" to="8"/>
    <selectFromSequence name="b" from="2" to="8"/>
    <selectFromSequence name="c" from="1" to="9"/>

    <math name="f">$a + $b x - x^2</math>

    <math name="f_c" simplify>$a + $b $c - $c^2</math>
    <math name="b_minus_two_c">$b - 2$c</math>

    <math name="ans" simplify="numbersPreserveOrder">($b - 2$c) - h</math>
    <math name="ans2" simplify="numbersPreserveOrder">- h + ($b - 2$c) </math>
  </setup>

<!-- testing -->
<!-- <p>ans = $ans</p>
<p>ans2 = $ans2</p> -->
<!-- testing -->

  <p>
    Let <m>f(x) = $f.</m> Find the difference quotient <m name="diffQuot">\frac{f($c+h)-f($c)}{h}</m>. Simplify your answer.
  </p>


    <p>
      <answer name="q1" symbolicEquality>
        <label><m>$diffQuot = </m></label>
        <award>$ans</award>
        <award>$ans2</award>
      </answer>
    </p>

  <givenAnswer>
    <p><m>$diffQuot = $ans</m></p>
  </givenAnswer>
  
</problem>


<!-- 
  <solution>
    <p>
      <alert>Step 1: Evaluate <m>f($c)</m> and <m>f($c+h)</m>.</alert><br />
      First, substitute <m>x = $c</m> into the original function:
      <me>f($c) = $a + $b($c) - ($c)^2 = $f_c</me>
    </p>
    <p>
      Next, substitute <m>x = $c+h</m> into the function and expand:
      <md>
        <mrow>f($c+h) &= $a + $b($c+h) - ($c+h)^2</mrow>
        <mrow>&= <math simplify name="fOf2plusH">$a + $b $c + $b h - ($c)^2 - 2$c h - h^2</math></mrow>
      </md>
    </p>

    <p>Now, subtract <m>f($c)</m> from <m>f($c+h)</m>:
      <me>f($c+h) - f($c) = $fOf2plusH - $f_c</me>
      Notice that the constant terms cancel out perfectly:
      <me>f($c+h) - f($c) = <math name="num" simplify>$fOf2plusH - $f_c</math></me>
    </p>

    <p>
      <alert>Step 3: Divide by <m>h</m> and simplify.</alert><br />
      Finally, divide the remaining numerator terms by <m>h</m>:
      <md>
        <mrow>\frac{f($c+h)-f($c)}{h} &= \frac{$num}{h}</mrow>
        <mrow>&= $ans</mrow>
      </md>
    </p>
  </solution> -->

<!-- 
